# wfe run bookkeeping. The scope node writes an intent record into the work
# item's checkout; it describes the run, not the product, so implement must not
# commit it into the branch it is building. Ignored so a slice PR carries only
# its engineering diff. See wfe_manager_artifacts.c (intent_self_referential).
.wfe-scope.json
intent_record_*.json
.rt-tmp/

# Local default output from `go build ./cmd/aimee-server` in the Go rewrite.
/server-go/aimee-server

# Session scratch working files (throwaway diffs, drivers, design drafts).
# The durable record lives in docs/proposals/ — 24 of these were committed to a
# branch by accident because nothing ignored them.
scratchpad/
/oidc-login-live
/write-tier-enforce-live

# Local public verification roots mounted read-only by the server Compose files.
# The directory is created by Docker on first use and must never be committed.
/server-management/

# Dogfood moment logs written by a test run. These are per-month jsonl files
# under a directory the dogfood config names; a suite run drops them wherever it
# is pointed. 26 got committed once, into directories whose names were
# UNINITIALISED STACK MEMORY (the dogfood_log_moment_live bug), and the invalid
# UTF-8 in those names broke the Docker build context for every e2e topology.
# Ignore them by shape so a stray run cannot be swept up by `git add -A` again.
**/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9].jsonl

# Scratch test harnesses. These drive real containers on a test host, are
# rewritten constantly while debugging, and are not part of the build. One of
# them reached the repo by accident (.stack-smoke.sh, in 7d64fdaf6) and a later
# `git add -A` swept in twenty more, which is why this ignores the shape rather
# than the filenames.
.stack-smoke.sh
.modelcache-test.sh
.hashcmp.sh
.hashcheck.sh
.ocicheck.sh
.health-probe.sh
.prefix-test.sh
.matrix-test.sh
.verify-ghcr.sh
.finish-move.sh
.move-containerd.sh
.restart-matrix.sh
.run-remote.sh
.unit.log
.upgrade-rehearsal/
.review-guide.md
.upgrade-*.sh
.start-*.sh
.ship.sh
.mt.tgz
.mt.b64

# Benchmark scratch: analysis scripts and deploy helpers for the ponytail codex
# comparison. These are working files for one investigation, not product code —
# they were committed by mistake and belong with the bench notes, not the repo.
/.deploytmp/
/*.py
/*.sh

# Transient deploy/sync bundles for the test container.
.synctmp/
src/.testlogs/
benchmarks/compaction-quality/.cache-ab/

# transient build/test logs written by local verification runs
.*.log

# scratch a local verification run writes beside the tree; committing one of
# these has happened twice, so they are named here rather than remembered
.commitmsg
.db2scratch/
.db2verify/
# Frozen diffs handed to roundtable review; regenerated per slice from git
# format-patch, so keeping them would commit a copy of the commit.
.review/
